Project Title: 12-Table Enterprise Data Model Optimization
Author: Data Analytics Team
Date: October 2026
Environment: Power BI Desktop / Power Query Editor
1. PROJECT OVERVIEW & OBJECTIVE
The primary objective of this project phase (Weeks 1–3) was to profile, validate, and integrate 12 separate structured data files into a high-performance, fully optimized Star Schema data model inside Power BI. This foundational setup guarantees rapid DAX engine processing, reliable filter propagation, and a clean directory for future executive report visualization.
2. DATA QUALITY AUDIT & TRANSFORMS
A comprehensive data profiling audit was conducted across all 12 tables using the Power Query Editor data profiling suite. The source files demonstrated an exceptionally high tier of baseline data integrity.
•	Data Quality Validation: Audited via the Column Quality tool. All core columns returned a metric of 100% Valid, 0% Empty, and 0% Errors, confirming total data completeness right from the source.
•	Structural Health: Designated Primary Keys across all lookup dimensions were profiled and verified to have 100% distinct and unique values, preventing any integrity faults across data relationships.
•	Applied Transformations (Visual Standardization): Because the structural data arrived in a pristine state, the only transformations applied were text polish operations. The 'Capitalize Each Word' function was systematically deployed on text fields (such as client names and geographic operating regions) to establish a uniform casing format across future dashboard visuals.
3. MASTER DATA DICTIONARY LOG
A. Customer Lookup Master (customers)
Table Type: Dimension (Lookup Table)
Description: Stores master demographic profiles for all registered organizational clients.
•	CustomerID (Text | Primary Key):  Unique alphanumeric identifier for each client. Audited to ensure 100% uniqueness.
•	CustomerName (Text):  Full corporate name of the client. Transformed using 'Capitalize Each Word'.
•	Region (Text):  Geographic operating territory. Transformed for uniform text casing.
B. Sales Order Lines Transaction Ledger (sales_orders_line)
Table Type: Fact (Transactional Table)
Description: Granular line-item records tracking individual product orders.
•	SalesOrderLineID (Text | Primary Key):  Unique row identifier.
•	SO_ID (Text | Foreign Key):  Synced and standardized to match the sales header table.
•	ProductID (Text | Foreign Key):  Connects directly to the product master table.
•	Quantity (Whole Number):  Number of units ordered per row.
•	Line Total (Currency):  Pre-calculated gross transactional value imported directly from the source.
•	Line Grand Total (Currency):  Pre-calculated final transactional value inclusive of adjustments.
4. ANALYTICAL DATA MODEL & RELATIONSHIP STRATEGY
To ensure high-speed DAX calculations and prevent ambiguous query pathways, the 12 files were integrated utilizing a strict Star Schema architecture.
•	Cardinality & Direction: Relationships are strictly structured as One-to-Many (1:*), flowing from master lookup tables down to transactional fact ledgers.
•	Filter Propagation: Cross-filter directions are set to 'Single' to ensure a deterministic, predictable flow of filtering data and avoid cyclic dependencies or calculation overhead.
